From: conda-forge
Subject: [PATCH] system: Define missing CLONE_NEWCGROUP flag for older kernels

CLONE_NEWCGROUP (clone()/unshare() cgroup namespace flag) was added to
the Linux kernel uapi in 4.6 (include/uapi/linux/sched.h). system/qemu-seccomp.c
uses it unconditionally via FORBID_CLONE_FLAG(CLONE_NEWCGROUP), but conda-forge's
pinned (older) sysroot kernel-uapi/glibc headers do not define it, causing a
build failure ("CLONE_NEWCGROUP" undeclared). Define it if missing, mirroring
the existing CLONE_PIDFD guard already present in this file.

diff --git a/system/qemu-seccomp.c b/system/qemu-seccomp.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/system/qemu-seccomp.c
+++ b/system/qemu-seccomp.c
@@ -59,6 +59,10 @@
 #ifndef CLONE_PIDFD
 # define CLONE_PIDFD 0x00001000
 #endif
+
+#ifndef CLONE_NEWCGROUP
+# define CLONE_NEWCGROUP 0x02000000
+#endif

 #define REQUIRE_CLONE_FLAG(flag) \
     const struct scmp_arg_cmp clone_arg ## flag[] = { \
